# Tomato-Butter Pasta

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1022464-tomato-butter-pasta) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251019015728/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1022464-tomato-butter-pasta))

{ rating="4" image="tomato_butter_pasta.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 lb [Cavatappi]{ ing="cavatappi" }, Rigatoni, Fettuccine
- [ ] 2-3 [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, halved horizontally (really need ripe and flavorful tomatoes)
- [ ] 4 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }, cold
- [ ] 1 large [garlic clove]{ ing="garlic-clove" }, peeled
- [ ] [Salt and Pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }, plus more for serving
- [ ] (Optional) [Torn basil leaves]{ ing="torn-basil-leaves" }, for serving
- [ ] [Parmesan]{ ing="parmesan" }, for serving

## Recipe

1. Start a pot to boil and cook the pasta. Make sure to reserve 1 cup pasta cooking water
1. Meanwhile, using the large holes of a box grater:

   1. Grate the cut ends of the [tomato]{ ing="tomatoes" } into a large bowl
   1. Grate the [butter]{ ing="butter" }
   1. Switch to the small holes and grate the garlic
1. Add the red-[pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" } and season generously with salt
1. Return the drained pasta to the pot, along with the bowl of grated [tomato]{ ing="tomatoes" } and [butter]{ ing="butter" }
1. Set over medium-high heat and stir constantly to thicken (2-3 min). Add pasta water as needed
1. Season to taste with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }. Serve with more red-[pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }, black pepper, basil and [Parmesan]{ ing="parmesan" } as desired
